!!!!! lab-c  192.168.1.30  scope lab  cisco (IOS-XE and IOS 15 syntax, RADIUS) !!!!!
! Based on the pull of <time> by alice over ssh (less than a minute ago; the login could see
! secrets) and the standard of <time> (tacctl 0.2.0-test). Lab-tested on IOS 12.4(15) (a
! 7200 emulator); other IOS trains and IOS-XE are written from the references.
! THIS OUTPUT HOLDS THE RADIUS KEY OF SCOPE lab: do not keep it in a file or a scrollback.
!
! What is irregular on lab-c (1 item; the paste fixes 1, leaves 0):
!  1. aaa      ACCESS     missing: radius server RADIUS: 4 statements (e.g. radius server RADIUS >
!                         address ipv4 10.0.0.77 auth-port 1645 acct-port 1813). Fixed by region lines
!                         4-7.
! Consistent: roles. Not planned: netconf, breakglass.
! The standard has nothing for: snmp, mgmt-acl.
! WARNING: the device has no enable secret: with the server unreachable, level 15 is reached only
! through the local user and 'aaa authorization exec'; set an enable secret first if you want a second
! way.
! WARNING: policy value not set: source interface (tacctl config cisco source-interface lab
! <interface>); the server matches this device by its source address.
! The change is live when the paste ends. NOTHING rolls it back by itself. Keep a second terminal
! logged in at privilege 15 until the end.
! Paste over ssh, not the console; on a console paste at most twenty lines at a time and watch the
! echo for '% Invalid'. Pasting the region twice is harmless.
!
! Type this first, on lab-c, and check the name:   show version | include uptime
! The prompt must end in # (privileged mode), not in (config)#, before you paste: a prompt ending in >
! means type enable first, a prompt with (config) in it means a configuration session is open: type
! end first.
!
!!!!! PASTE FROM HERE: lab-c !!!!!
configure terminal
! aaa: tacctl's RADIUS server block
radius server RADIUS
 address ipv4 10.0.0.77 auth-port 1645 acct-port 1813
 key lab-secret-0123456789abcdef
 timeout 5
 retransmit 2
end
!!!!! PASTE TO HERE: lab-c !!!!!
!
! If any line printed "% Invalid" or "% Error", stop and undo it: tacctl device config plan lab-c
! --backout (its own region, to paste in the second terminal).
!
! Check now (nothing rolls this back by itself):
!   From the tacctl server:   tacctl device config pull lab-c --diff     (aaa: ok)
!   In the second terminal:   open a NEW ssh session to lab-c as yourself, then: terminal length 0, show privilege (must say 15)
! When both checks are fine, type this one command yourself:  write memory
!
! To undo: tacctl device config plan lab-c --backout (tacctl keeps this plan's back-out: after the
! check pull has replaced the picture, the command still prints this plan's, and says which pull
! it undoes, until the next plan with changes)
! Do not: 'write memory' before the check; paste outside the banners; paste into another device;
! paste on a console more than twenty lines at a time; keep this output in a file after the paste
! when it holds a secret.
! Locked out (the paste cut your session and no login works)? A superuser runs: tacctl breakglass hold lab-c --reason "..."
! then log in as the device's local account (console: local login, then 'enable' with the local secret),
! fix or back out, and the superuser runs: tacctl breakglass release lab-c
